.TH "WILE" "1" "November 2026" "wile 0.4.261112" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
wile \[en] prescriptive task dispatcher for Ruby gem projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[V]wile [<task>] [<args>...] [:<options>...]\f[R]
.PP
\f[V]wile <options>...\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]Wile\f[R] is a prescriptive task dispatcher for Ruby gem projects,
built around a living project template.
.PP
It scaffolds new projects from the template, keeps existing ones aligned
with it, and automates workflow steps \[en] gemspec upkeep, testing, and
release.
.SH GET STARTED
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]wile\f[R]: Display manual page.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]wile <options>...\f[R]: Query options dictionary for flag details.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]wile list\f[R]: List all available tasks.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]wile help [<task>]\f[R]: Show help for task(s).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]wile test [<file> [<method>]]\f[R]: Run project test suites.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-h\f[R], \f[V]--help\f[R]: Show help summary.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-v\f[R], \f[V]--version\f[R]: Show version number.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-a\f[R], \f[V]--all\f[R]: Apply to all targets.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]--batch\f[R]: Run in non-interactive batch mode.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-c\f[R], \f[V]--check\f[R]: Run in check-only mode.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-d\f[R], \f[V]--dump\f[R]: Dump internal structure or data.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-f\f[R], \f[V]--force\f[R]: Force execution without safety checks.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]--format=WORD\f[R]: Output format.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-l\f[R], \f[V]--list\f[R]: List items.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]--name=WORD\f[R]: Filter or match by name.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]--only=CSV\f[R]: Select only specified items.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-q\f[R], \f[V]--quiet\f[R]: Suppress non-essential output.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-r\f[R], \f[V]--raw\f[R]: Raw / unformatted output.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-s\f[R], \f[V]--strict\f[R]: Enable strict mode.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-t\f[R], \f[V]--trace\f[R]: Trace execution.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]-y\f[R], \f[V]--yes\f[R]: Answer yes to all prompts.
.SH TASKS
.PP
Run \f[V]wile list\f[R] to list all tasks, or \f[V]wile help <task>\f[R]
for details.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]build\f[R]: Build gem package (see \f[B]BUILD\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]bump\f[R]: Bump project version number.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]compare\f[R]: Compare project files with template (see
\f[B]COMPARE\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]content\f[R]: Inspect ruby file structure and methods (see
\f[B]CONTENT\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]cp\f[R]: Copy template files into project (see \f[B]CP\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]dependencies\f[R]: List ruby dependencies.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]dictionary\f[R]: Manage spelling dictionary (see
\f[B]DICTIONARY\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]gemcheck\f[R]: Check for missing gems across rbenv Rubies (see
\f[B]GEMCHECK\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]gemfile\f[R]: Generate Gemfile from dependencies (see
\f[B]GEMFILE\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]help\f[R]: Show detailed help for tasks (see \f[B]HELP\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]info\f[R]: Display project metadata and configuration (see
\f[B]INFO\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]install\f[R]: Build and install gem locally (see
\f[B]INSTALL\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]lexicon\f[R]: View and update vocabulary whitelist (see
\f[B]LEXICON\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]list\f[R]: List all tasks or filter by pattern (see
\f[B]LIST\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]mkdir\f[R]: Create project directory from template (see
\f[B]MKDIR\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]note\f[R]: Scrape ruby files for NOTE comments (see
\f[B]NOTE\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]nvim\f[R]: Open project files in Neovim (see \f[B]NVIM\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]order\f[R]: Suggest method ordering in ruby files (see
\f[B]ORDER\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]publish\f[R]: Publish new version to RubyGems.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]requirements\f[R]: Verify system commands and versions.
